A||N||14||Springtyme||Practical car? I think not...||||5||
Z||000000||Springtyme||09-07-2001||09:48 AM||||Okay, so here's a question for all you people out there who own a Fiero and do the grocery shopping. Where do you put the groceries?!?!?!? You can't put anything that needs to be refrigerated or put in the freezer in the back cause it gets too warm. Ice cream melts and what not.... okay, so I put them on the passenger seat and floor, but what if you have a passenger???? I'm just trying to figure this out... Any help?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Springtyme.jpg"> <P>            ~Springtyme~||||reg||5
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||09-07-2001||09:54 AM||||Nobody said the Fiero was good for grocery shopping  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  -If I take the Fiero, that means a limited supply run: 3 bags + Passenger is all that will fit up front... then whatever else you can fit in the trunk that won't melt or cook.<P>I usually take our '92 Toyota Camry, or my '94 Olds Bravada... lots more space in those.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg"> <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero5||09-07-2001||10:08 AM||||What? have you people must have been sitting near your exhaust too long?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"> <P>Marian does her shopping for 5 people every week in her 88. Nothing get's spoiled or melted, and she hits 2 to 3 places.<BR>She does get alot of onlookers in the parking lot who watch to see if she will be able to get everything in her Fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>Steve<P><P>------------------<BR>                               <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pegasuswarriersSig.jpg">                            <BR>http://www.kelleyfamilyfieros.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||6
Z||000003||Alex4mula||09-07-2001||10:24 AM||||Same here. I have had over $200 worth of groceries in my car. The front can hold couple bags specially cold items near the A/C can. I moved twice with only my Fiero. Have carried 19" inch TVs and sofa on top among other things. It can hold lot more than what you expect by looking its size.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Springtyme||09-07-2001||10:36 AM||||I was wishing i had bungee cords with me yesterday so I could put stuff on the roof rack. I wasn't sure if the cold things would get warm in the back, so I didn't even chance it. Hmmm... I guess I know now =) Thanks!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Springtyme.jpg"> <P>            ~Springtyme~||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||09-07-2001||11:41 AM||||Sometimes I put the cold stuff in the back, but I only live a mile from the store. Usually not the frozen stuff, though.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||6
Z||000006||Tina||09-07-2001||11:57 AM||||Well in all honesty the Fiero is perhaps not the most practical car.<BR>Don't worry though, your just getting used to it.<BR>It takes a while to figure out where to but what. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>But yes bungee-cords are always good, and one of those thermal Freezer bags to keep things cold longer,isn't a bad idea either.<P>Tina<BR>BTW  Yes, popcicles go next to the mastercylinder.Flowers, veggies,and stuff in the passenger seat.Dry goods in the trunk.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cheever3000||09-07-2001||11:59 AM||||I do the grocery shopping for my family of five... and two of them are teenage boys (and then there's <B>my</B> voracious appetite)!  I haven't had a problem with cold things in the back, it's sealed pretty well from the engine.  The stores I shop at are about two miles away.<P>Just put the heavy stuff in the bottom.  Fruit & cereal in the middle.  Chips & bread on top.  Eggs in the passenger's lap.  <P>It's great when old men bring my groceries out to the car with me.  They enjoy talking about it, and of course so do I.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000008||artherd||09-07-2001||06:29 PM||||I've had all kinds of things in my car, including a Lowell film lighting rig. (the whole thing. plus several 2k HMIs.)<P>I've done the grocery bit too, I figure if I can't fit it all in, I can just make three or so trips, and learn the course.  I MEAN road... a little better.<P>It is amazing what you can fit in the car, and no the rear dosen't get terribly warm, but I only have a 5mile ride.  <P>Most of the room is in the passanger seat, yay!<P>PS: asking me where the cupholders are, how much mileage I get, or about cargo space, are just the wrong questions  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000009||Fformula88||09-07-2001||11:15 PM||||What!?!?  Take the Fiero near a parking lot full of shopping carts?!?!?!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><P>NEVER!!!<P>Ok, so I don't do ANY grocery shopping... but if I did and needed to keep things cool I would go to a store close to home and drive VERY fast before it all melted!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierosig2.JPG"> <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000010||artherd||09-08-2001||01:34 AM||||Oh, I forgot to mention, I always park at the car stereo shop down the street, heh!<P>Shoping carts + idoits == The Badlands.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fformula88:<BR><B>What!?!?  Take the Fiero near a parking lot full of shopping carts?!?!?!   <BR>NEVER!!!<P>Ok, so I don't do ANY grocery shopping... but if I did and needed to keep things cool I would go to a store close to home and drive VERY fast before it all melted!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000011||LZeitgeist||09-08-2001||08:21 AM||||The Catch-22...<P>With a trunk full of ice cream, do you:<P>A) Drive really fast to get home quick, but create more intense engine heat? or<P>B) Drive really slow so the engine doesn't heat up as much, but for a longer amount of time?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>(No, you don't really have to answer this... everyone knows the answer is really<P>C) Eat your ice cream in the grocery store parking lot while you're talking to all the 'closet Fiero fans' and the gawkers wondering why you have an engine in your trunk...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">)||||reg||1
Z||000012||Archie||09-08-2001||09:12 AM||||Easy answer, Eat out!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Archie||||reg||1
Z||000013||Haagster||09-08-2001||02:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B>Easy answer, Eat out!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Archie</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Or Domino's Pizza<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_4.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000014||Veronica's V6 GT||09-08-2001||10:01 PM||||I use my Fiero all the time when I go grocery shopping. A full cart of groceries have always fit into the trunk.  It takes me 10-15 minutes to get home and I've never had anything thaw or spoil.  I load it starting with the heavy stuff on the bottom, light things on the top and the cold things in the middle, it insulates them that way.  On 80-90 degree days things will thaw just as quickly in other trunks as well, I don't think theirs are much cooler than a Fiero.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>88 GT<BR></UL><P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Vonnies.jpg"> ||||reg||1
